    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d109">

                <pb facs="0513" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg499"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCulloch, collector, to Captain Webster.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Custom-House,
                            Baltimore</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Collector’s
                        Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1819-12-03"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">December</hi> 3, 1819</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Upon receiving this be pleased to attend
                    the South American schooner El Ameida till she goes out of the Chesapeake. You
                    will anchor near her when she anchors, and keep off all boats or vessels
                    visiting her and prevent anything being *carried on board her from the water or
                    land side that will add to her military strength. <pb facs="0514" n="500"
                        xml:id="pg500"/> The necessary supplies of fresh provisions and water and
                    vegetables are not intended to be denied, but men and warlike stores must be
                    driven off or seized. <seg type="margin">[132]</seg></p>
                <p>If the inspector meet you he will give you the commission and clearance of the
                    vessel, which you will please deliver to her commander at her departure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>J. H. McCULLOCH.</item>
                            <item>Captain <hi rendition="#small-caps">John A. Webster.</hi></item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
